{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAG6SkpgkBzMAzyCH5hS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I narrowed the `Hijack` check in `response_writer.go`. It used to refuse whenever `Written()` was true, which included the case where only the headers had gone out. Websocket libraries such as coder/websocket send headers before they hijack, so they were being blocked. Now `Hijack` refuses only once body bytes have been written (`size > 0`).\n\nI added a test case in `response_writer_test.go`: calling `WriteHeaderNow()` and then `Hijack()` should succeed. The existing case that expects hijacking after a body write to fail still passes. GATE PASS: the new test fails without the change and passes with it, and the format and leftover checks are clean.\n\nI only ran the `TestResponseWriterHijack*` tests, not the full suite, and I didn't test against a real websocket library."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1204,"cache_read_input_tokens":34085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1204,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3af47898-1105-4a32-aeb6-65bc41b9a5a1","uuid":"e0ff794f-582c-4016-9882-9e4a5a318b87","timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:33:14.342Z","request_id":"req_011CgAG6SZAhHsjPfYZWRdTv"}
